      "content": "hey so i need some help or maybe just to talk through something bc im kinda freaking out. i was doing that internship at the lab last month (the particle accelerator wing) and there was this weird surge in the stream, like it wasn't supposed to happen. ever since then i've been seeing these weird colors in my peripheral vision. like, if something bad is about to happen, i see these heavy red clouds before it even occurs. it's not like a hallucination i can just dismiss, it feels like i'm actually seeing the density of what's coming next. do you think there's any way this could be linked to the particle exposure? like, could it have actually changed how my brain processes probability?",
