      "content": "i already went to a doctor and they basically told me it was just stress or eye strain, so they didn't think anything of it. but they don't understand what it's actually like. it's not just light—it's like a mathematical certainty. like i saw this deep crimson haze around a coworker yesterday right before he tripped and broke his arm, and it wasn't just a coincidence. i feel like my brain has been tuned to a different frequency because of that particle stream. if you look at the physics of quantum superposition or how wave functions collapse, isn't it possible that i'm just perceiving the probability field before it fully manifests? like, instead of seeing the event, i'm seeing the weight of the possibility?",
